Create one real downloadable file. Supported standalone UTF-8 text extensions: {{ supported_text_extensions | join(', ') }}. Preserve the requested filename and extension; these text files do not need a ZIP. Call once per requested file. Use .zip only when the user explicitly requests an archive. Also supports .docx, .pdf, .xlsx and .pptx. For .docx/.pdf use plain text or JSON {'blocks':[{'type':'heading'|'paragraph','text':'...'}, {'type':'table','rows':[['A','B']]}]}. For .xlsx use {'sheets':[{'name':'Sheet1','rows':[['A',1]]}]}; .pptx use {'slides':[{'title':'Title','body':'Text'}]}; .zip use {'entries':[{'name':'notes.txt','content':'Text'}]}. Text formats take their raw UTF-8 content, not Markdown fences or archive JSON. For images use generate_image instead; do not generate executables.
